From: Alan Shearer
Subject: net_server: restore static default route when the interface goes up

ifconfig down invalidates every route on the interface, including
RTF_DEFAULT. ifconfig up only rebuilds the host and subnet routes from
InterfaceAddress. The saved gateway lives in the interfaces file and is
installed only from _ConfigureInterface (boot, settings write, or a new
/dev/net node). IFF_UP is not one of those paths.

Watch B_NETWORK_INTERFACE_CHANGED. On a down-to-up transition, if the
profile is static and still has a gateway, add that default route again.
Leave DHCP / auto_config alone.

Coldfirex/haiku-fixes#1
https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/9695
https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/16349

